{"from": "Artobiography Docket <signals@nariway.com>", "to": ["alina@nariway.com"], "subject": "Artobiography docket - the Phillips settles, a Mondrian surfaces after 70 years, 10 more", "html": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com\">\n<link rel=\"preconnect\" href=\"https://fonts.gstatic.com\" crossorigin>\n<link href=\"https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Newsreader:ital,opsz,wght@0,6..72,400;0,6..72,500;0,6..72,600;1,6..72,400&family=Manrope:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap\" rel=\"stylesheet\">\n<title>Artobiography Docket</title>\n</head>\n<body style=\"margin:0; padding:0; background-color:#FFFFFF; font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;\">\n<div style=\"width:100%; max-width:600px; margin:0 auto; padding:32px 20px 48px 20px; background-color:#FFFFFF;\">\n\n  <!-- MASTHEAD -->\n  <div style=\"margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:24px; line-height:1.2; color:#1A1A17; font-weight:600; letter-spacing:0.01em;\">Artobiography Docket</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:13px; line-height:1.5; color:#6B6B62; margin-top:4px; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.12em;\">Thursday, August 27, 2026</div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; margin:20px 0 24px 0;\"></div>\n\n  <!-- ORIENTATION -->\n  <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:17px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0 0 12px 0;\">\n    Twelve candidates from the past week of Signals, strongest first. This is a research menu, not a drafted edition &mdash; select 4&ndash;6 for the newsletter.\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; margin:0 0 32px 0;\"></div>\n\n  <!-- ITEM 1 -->\n  <div style=\"margin:0 0 30px 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:12px; line-height:1.4; color:#6B6B62; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">01 &middot; Governance and durability</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:21px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Phillips Collection ends its 18-month &ldquo;core collection&rdquo; fight</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      An agreement with its board of members redefines &ldquo;core collection&rdquo; to cover the full 1985 catalogue rather than the narrower 1999 list. The ten works already headed to Sotheby&rsquo;s (O&rsquo;Keeffe, Seurat, Kapoor) can now be sold; everything else in the broader catalogue is now permanently protected. Aug 26, 2026.\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#4A4A44; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      <strong>Related:</strong> Phillips Collection (coded case) &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <strong>Verification:</strong> verified\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A;\">\n      Resolving this gives other collector-founded institutions a template for redrawing a founder&rsquo;s holdings without full litigation.\n      <br>\n      <a href=\"https://www.phillipscollection.org/sites/default/files/2026-02/phillips-collection-management-policy.pdf\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">Phillips Collection policy (primary) &rarr;</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://hyperallergic.com/why-is-dc-phillips-collection-selling-off-its-masterpieces/\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">Hyperallergic &rarr;</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; margin:0 0 28px 0;\"></div>\n\n  <!-- ITEM 2 -->\n  <div style=\"margin:0 0 30px 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:12px; line-height:1.4; color:#6B6B62; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">02 &middot; Estate planning / disperse</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:21px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Christie&rsquo;s and Sotheby&rsquo;s openly fighting over the Herbert Lust estate</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      Herbert Lust, who died in May 2026 at 99, spent seven decades assembling over 1,000 works (deep Giacometti, plus Indiana, Bellmer, Stella). His estate is shopping ~300 pieces worth about $60M between the two biggest houses; he had already donated hundreds of works to museums during his lifetime. Reported Aug 20, 2026.\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#4A4A44; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      <strong>Related:</strong> Herbert Lust Collection (coded case) &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <strong>Verification:</strong> verified\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A;\">\n      A consignment fought over openly is a visible marker of what happens when a lifetime distribution plan stops partway through.\n      <br>\n      <a href=\"https://www.artnews.com/art-news/market/christies-sothebys-battle-herbert-lust-collection-1234795281/\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">ARTnews (primary) &rarr;</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://robbreport.com/shelter/art-collectibles/christies-sothebys-herbert-lust-art-holdings-1238570046/\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">Robb Report &rarr;</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; margin:0 0 28px 0;\"></div>\n\n  <!-- ITEM 3 -->\n  <div style=\"margin:0 0 30px 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:12px; line-height:1.4; color:#6B6B62; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">03 &middot; Public-access models</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:21px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Amanda Precourt&rsquo;s Cookie Factory profiled as the anti-vanity-museum case</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      Denver collector Amanda Precourt converted a condemned fortune-cookie factory into a free 5,000+ sq ft public art space with Jérôme Sans as artistic director; she lives above it with her own collection. Elisa Carollo&rsquo;s Aug 25 Observer profile frames it explicitly against the founder&rsquo;s-monument museum model. Space opened May 2025.\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#4A4A44; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      <strong>Related:</strong> Cookie Factory Denver (coded case) &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <strong>Verification:</strong> verified\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A;\">\n      A living collector publicly rejecting the founder&rsquo;s-monument model is a useful counterweight to the mega-museum pathway this docket tracks most often.\n      <br>\n      <a href=\"https://www.artspell.media/p/august-25-2026\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">Art Spell roundup (primary) &rarr;</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://coloradosun.com/2025/05/23/new-art-center-debuts-in-an-old-denver-fortune-cookie-factory/\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">The Colorado Sun &rarr;</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; margin:0 0 28px 0;\"></div>\n\n  <!-- ITEM 4 -->\n  <div style=\"margin:0 0 30px 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:12px; line-height:1.4; color:#6B6B62; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">04 &middot; Disperse / sale</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:21px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Sandy Lerner&rsquo;s cat-art collection gets firm dispersal dates at Bonhams</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      Cisco co-founder Sandy Lerner&rsquo;s three-decade cat-art collection now has confirmed dates: an online leg Sept 22&ndash;Oct 1 and a live sale Sept 30 at Bonhams&rsquo; new New York flagship, 66 lots including a Foujita and a Giacometti. No foundation, no museum &mdash; a plain single-owner dispersal. Confirmed Aug 26&ndash;27, 2026.\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#4A4A44; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      <strong>Related:</strong> none yet &mdash; candidate to add &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <strong>Verification:</strong> verified\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A;\">\n      A cleanly personal collection choosing straightforward sale over any legacy vehicle is a counterweight to this docket&rsquo;s museum-heavy sample.\n      <br>\n      <a href=\"https://www.artnews.com/art-news/news/sandy-lerner-cat-themed-art-collection-auctioned-bonhams-1234795289/\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">ARTnews (primary) &rarr;</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.artsy.net/article/artsy-editorial-major-collection-cat-related-art-collectibles-heads-bonhams-auction-fall\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">Artsy &rarr;</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; margin:0 0 28px 0;\"></div>\n\n  <!-- ITEM 5 -->\n  <div style=\"margin:0 0 30px 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:12px; line-height:1.4; color:#6B6B62; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">05 &middot; Valuation / deaccessioning</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:21px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">The Met recycles a decade-old Irving gift into its own acquisitions fund</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      Sotheby&rsquo;s will offer 300+ Chinese works &mdash; jades, Buddhist sculpture, porcelain &mdash; across two Asia Week sales (Sept 10 and 14), all originally given to the Met in 2015 by Florence and Herbert Irving. Proceeds fund an Irving acquisitions endowment; this continues an established sale series rather than a one-off. Reported Aug 27, 2026.\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#4A4A44; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      <strong>Related:</strong> none yet &mdash; candidate to add &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <strong>Verification:</strong> verified\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A;\">\n      A museum recycling a gift into its own acquisitions fund, with the family&rsquo;s apparent blessing, is a different shape of deaccessioning than the funding-crisis cases usually logged.\n      <br>\n      <a href=\"https://www.artsy.net/article/artsy-editorial-metropolitan-museum-will-sell-300-works-chinese-art-sothebys\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">Artsy (primary) &rarr;</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.sothebys.com/en/series/chinese-art-from-the-metropolitan-museum-of-art-the-florence-and-herbert-irving-gift\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">Sotheby&rsquo;s &rarr;</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; margin:0 0 28px 0;\"></div>\n\n  <!-- ITEM 6 -->\n  <div style=\"margin:0 0 30px 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:12px; line-height:1.4; color:#6B6B62; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">06 &middot; The market / disperse</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:21px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">A Mondrian held by one family for 70 years surfaces at Christie&rsquo;s</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      Armand Bartos bought <em>Composition III</em> (1920) in 1950 and held it with his wife Celeste until 1973; never once at public auction. It leads Christie&rsquo;s Frieze Week evening sale (London, Oct 14), estimated &pound;20&ndash;30M. Reported Aug 26&ndash;27, 2026.\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#4A4A44; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      <strong>Related:</strong> none yet &mdash; candidate to add &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <strong>Verification:</strong> verified\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A;\">\n      A work released by the family that held it, rather than by an estate after a death, illustrates a slower and more deliberate route to market.\n      <br>\n      <a href=\"https://www.artnews.com/art-news/market/mondrian-painting-auction-christies-frieze-week-1234795778/\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">ARTnews (primary) &rarr;</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://news.artnet.com/market/piet-mondrian-auction-christies-london-2802907\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">Artnet &rarr;</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; margin:0 0 28px 0;\"></div>\n\n  <!-- ITEM 7 -->\n  <div style=\"margin:0 0 30px 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:12px; line-height:1.4; color:#6B6B62; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">07 &middot; Estate planning / succession</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:21px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Las Vegas Museum of Art&rsquo;s opening slips again, to fall 2029</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      The opening has moved from a previously stated 2028 target to fall 2029 &mdash; the first concrete timeline news since founder Elaine Wynn&rsquo;s death in April 2025. A smaller media-lab prelude opens spring 2026 in the meantime. Reported Aug 22, 2026.\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#4A4A44; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      <strong>Related:</strong> Las Vegas Museum of Art (coded case) &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <strong>Verification:</strong> single-source\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A;\">\n      A second slip since its founder&rsquo;s death is worth tracking as a case of what a founder-driven museum&rsquo;s timeline does once the founder is no longer there.\n      <br>\n      <a href=\"https://www.reviewjournal.com/business/future-las-vegas-art-museum-unveils-plans-for-media-lab-3392100/\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">Las Vegas Review-Journal (primary) &rarr;</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; margin:0 0 28px 0;\"></div>\n\n  <!-- ITEM 8 -->\n  <div style=\"margin:0 0 30px 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:12px; line-height:1.4; color:#6B6B62; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">08 &middot; Partner &mdash; scholarly infrastructure</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:21px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Klesch Collection endows an art-history-and-AI fellowship</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      Anita and A. Gary Klesch, whose collection holds 15th- to 17th-century European art (Arcimboldo, van Dyck, Rubens), are funding a two-year postdoctoral fellowship at Birkbeck, University of London, on art history, AI, and digital heritage &mdash; instead of expanding a building. Reported Aug 20, 2026.\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#4A4A44; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      <strong>Related:</strong> Klesch Collection &mdash; Birkbeck (coded case) &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <strong>Verification:</strong> single-source\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A;\">\n      Funding scholarly infrastructure rather than a building is a legacy vehicle this docket sees less often.\n      <br>\n      <a href=\"https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/08/20/klesch-collection-endow-postdoctoral-fellowship-focusing-art-history-ai-birkbeck-london\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">The Art Newspaper (primary) &rarr;</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; margin:0 0 28px 0;\"></div>\n\n  <!-- ITEM 9 -->\n  <div style=\"margin:0 0 30px 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:12px; line-height:1.4; color:#6B6B62; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">09 &middot; Governance and durability</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:21px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Art Omi&rsquo;s shared-campus pavilions flagged as a taxonomy problem</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      Art Omi&rsquo;s 190-acre Chatham, NY campus &mdash; 12 to 18 collectors and artists each design and control their own legacy pavilion &mdash; was reassessed this week as not fitting any of the six standing pathway families. A &ldquo;shared-campus&rdquo; proposal is pending. Phase One opens June 2027. Flagged in Signals Aug 23, 2026.\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#4A4A44; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      <strong>Related:</strong> none yet &mdash; case deferred pending pathway-family decision &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <strong>Verification:</strong> verified\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A;\">\n      A shared-campus model where each participant controls one pavilion may be reason enough to treat it as its own case type.\n      <br>\n      <a href=\"https://artomipavilions.org/\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">Art Omi Pavilions (primary) &rarr;</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.archpaper.com/2024/07/art-omi-debuts-new-architect-and-artist-designed-pavilions-in-chatham-new-york/\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">The Architect&rsquo;s Newspaper &rarr;</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; margin:0 0 28px 0;\"></div>\n\n  <!-- ITEM 10 -->\n  <div style=\"margin:0 0 30px 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:12px; line-height:1.4; color:#6B6B62; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">10 &middot; Build</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:21px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Eduardo Costantini times a Malba expansion to its 25th anniversary</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      Malba founder Eduardo Costantini&rsquo;s Dec 2025 acquisition of the 1,233-work Daros Latinamerica collection anchors a building extension beneath Plaza Perú, roughly doubling the museum&rsquo;s footprint, timed to its 25th anniversary this September. Surfaced in Signals Aug 22, 2026; underlying deal is not new this week.\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#4A4A44; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      <strong>Related:</strong> none yet &mdash; candidate to add &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <strong>Verification:</strong> verified\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A;\">\n      A living founder timing a footprint expansion to an anniversary is familiar, here at unusually large scale for a Latin American institution.\n      <br>\n      <a href=\"https://www.artnews.com/art-news/news/malba-acquires-daros-latinamerica-collection-expansion-1234766956/\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">ARTnews (primary) &rarr;</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2025/12/17/museo-arte-latinoamericano-buenos-aires-acquires-daros-latinamerica-collection\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">The Art Newspaper &rarr;</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; margin:0 0 28px 0;\"></div>\n\n  <!-- ITEM 11 -->\n  <div style=\"margin:0 0 30px 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:12px; line-height:1.4; color:#6B6B62; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">11 &middot; Public-access models</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:21px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Ken Griffin&rsquo;s Leonardo hangs quietly at the Met, on loan</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      <em>Madonna of the Yarnwinder</em> (studio of Leonardo, c. 1505), owned by Ken Griffin, has hung at the Met since spring 2026 with no announcement, only a new wall label. Reported Aug 20, 2026.\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#4A4A44; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      <strong>Related:</strong> none yet &mdash; candidate to add &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <strong>Verification:</strong> verified\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A;\">\n      A loan that generated a wall label rather than a press release is a quieter, more reversible pathway than most gift and foundation stories tracked here.\n      <br>\n      <a href=\"https://www.artnews.com/art-news/news/met-museum-leonardo-da-vinci-ken-griffin-1234794238/\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">ARTnews (primary) &rarr;</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://puck.news/newsletter_content/ken-griffins-stealth-leonardo-the-mets-orientalism-show/\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">Puck &rarr;</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; margin:0 0 28px 0;\"></div>\n\n  <!-- ITEM 12 -->\n  <div style=\"margin:0 0 12px 0;\">\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:12px; line-height:1.4; color:#6B6B62; text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.1em; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">12 &middot; Public-access models &mdash; countertrend</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Newsreader',Georgia,'Times New Roman',serif; font-size:21px; line-height:1.3; color:#1A1A17; font-weight:600; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">Yusaku Maezawa&rsquo;s superyacht carries a two-story private gallery</div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      Maezawa took delivery of the <em>Nausicaä</em>, a $350M, 375-foot superyacht with a two-story revolving gallery of Warhol, Koons, Prince, and Wool. Entirely private, no public access. Reported Aug 19&ndash;20, 2026.\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#4A4A44; margin:0 0 8px 0;\">\n      <strong>Related:</strong> none yet &mdash; countertrend marker, no public access &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp; <strong>Verification:</strong> verified\n    </div>\n    <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:15px; line-height:1.6; color:#0A0A0A;\">\n      A private space built for mobility runs counter to nearly every other item here &mdash; a reminder that public access is a choice, not a default.\n      <br>\n      <a href=\"https://news.artnet.com/art-world/art-collector-yusaku-maezawa-superyacht-2798941\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">Artnet (primary) &rarr;</a> &nbsp;&middot;&nbsp;\n      <a href=\"https://www.artnews.com/art-news/market/bruce-museum-chief-curator-yusaku-maezawa-yacht-industry-moves-1234795285/\" style=\"color:#1A1A17; text-decoration:underline;\">ARTnews &rarr;</a>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div style=\"border-top:1px solid #E7E5DF; margin:32px 0 20px 0;\"></div>\n\n  <div style=\"font-family:'Manrope','Schibsted Grotesk',system-ui,-apple-system,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; font-size:13px; line-height:1.6; color:#6B6B62;\">\n    Six items have no matching Nariway collection record yet: Sandy Lerner, the Met&rsquo;s Irving deaccession, the Bartos Collection, Art Omi Pavilions, Ken Griffin&rsquo;s Leonardo loan, and Maezawa&rsquo;s yacht gallery. This is the weekly research menu, not the drafted edition &mdash; a full docket with dates, sources, and notes is in the vault at artobiography/dockets/2026-08-27.md.\n  </div>\n\n</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n"}